h+='</tbody></table></div><p>Cases have equal weight. A clear speed observation requires at least 5% difference and disjoint observed ranges. Overlapping variation counts as a tie.</p><h2>Node profile comparison</h2><p class="notice">Node uses 44.1 kHz float WAV and lamejs MP3. Its DSP, encoder, sample count and fsync behavior differ. Its time and memory ratios below describe the observed export; they are excluded from the matched-workload aggregate.</p>'
h+=f"<p>Node geometric mean Zig / Node time: {fmt(node['geomean_speedup'])}. Median sampled RSS / Zig: {fmt(node['median_memory_ratio'])}.</p>"
h+='''<h2>Case measurements</h2><div id="filters"></div><p id="count" aria-live="polite"></p><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Case</th><th>Entry</th><th>Median s</th><th>IQR s</th><th>Min–max s</th><th>Input s / s</th><th>Zig / entry</th><th>Observation</th><th>Tree RSS bytes</th><th>RSS / Zig</th><th>RSS delta bytes</th><th>Tree CPU s</th></tr></thead><tbody id="data"></tbody></table></div><p><a href="cases.csv">Download all case measurements</a> · <a href="performance-gates.csv">Export qualification</a> · <a href="memory-processes.json">Concurrent memory breakdown</a></p><h2>Method and limits</h2><p>192 cases cross 20 ms, 1 s, 60 s, 600 s, 2 × 30 s and 16 × 3.75 s inputs; WAV/MP3 input and output; ratios 0.5/1/1.255/2; fresh/overwrite publication. One untimed warmup precedes seven rotated speed runs and a separate sampled memory pass. Startup through final publication and process exit is timed.</p><p>RSS sums simultaneously sampled wrapper and child resident memory, including validators. The sampler waits 2 ms after each scan and records actual cadence. Brief peaks may be missed and shared mappings may be counted more than once. It is neither wrapper-only RSS nor the sum of unrelated per-process maxima. Memory passes do not enter speed medians.</p><p>Other sessions and a busy single-core Python process remained active. Host load and swap were recorded. Filesystem caches were not purged; separate first-launch measurements do not establish disk-cold latency. This is macOS arm64 evidence, with no physical listening or second-device access claim.</p><details><summary>Builds and dependencies</summary><pre>'''+esc(json.dumps(json.loads((c.WORK/'builds.json').read_text()),indent=2))+'''</pre></details><p><a href="REPORT.md">Read all findings and reproduction details</a> · <a href="fixtures.json">Fixture hashes</a> · <a href="config.json">Pinned revisions and environment</a></p></main><script>'''
